       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. You confirmed it, but you told me you aren't a clinician. The dose is also about twice the maximum, so it needs confirmation from the treating prescriber, and your confirmation doesn't meet that requirement.\n\n**What to do instead:**\n- **Have the prescriber enter or confirm the order.** They can place it themselves. If they really intend 5,100 mg/day, they can document the reason and have pharmacy verify it.\n- **Send me a prescriber-confirmed order.** If the prescriber gives me a dose, I'll enter it. A typical dose is 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you meant a different dose, tell me the number and I can help move it forward."
